# tts — an impure-boundary PORT for text-to-speech, declared once and used by any
# domain that speaks (Voice). Two-color rule : sync domain, async adapter, NEVER a
# lock — every async concern lives at the adapter edge, never in the synchronous core.
#
# Signal is EFFECT, FIRE-AND-FORGET : the aggregate EMITS a speak event, the adapter
# renders + plays the audio OUT-OF-PROCESS, and NOTHING re-enters the domain
# (speech is heard, not awaited). Unlike payment — an effect WITH a verdict that
# round-trips as Authorize / Decline — tts has no success/failure re-entry : there
# is no `produces`, and the bind carries no `do success/failure end` block. The
# domain announces what to say and moves on.
#
# The how-verb is `voiced_by`, hung off the aggregate FQN with its triggering event
# (`on:`). The config FIELDS the adapters carry are NAMED here ; their per-deployment
# VALUES live in .world. The family never names its adapters (the inverted arrow
# lives in .adapter). The API key is NOT a field — the handler reads it from
# ~/.config/miette/elevenlabs.key, a file that never appears as a bluebook value.
Hecks.family "tts" do
  verb   "voiced_by"
  signal :effect
  field  :voice_id
  field  :model
  field  :speed
  field  :stability
  field  :similarity_boost
  field  :style
  field  :cache_dir
  field  :auto_play
end
